    <h2>Building Good Nutrition Tips</h2>
<article>
<h3>Why Does it Matter</h3>
<figure>
    <img src="Nutritous Food.webp" alt="A plate filled with fruits and veggies" width="250" height="250">
    <figcaption>
        A nutritous meal consists of protien, fruits, veggies, and <b>lots</b> of water.
    </figcaption>
</figure>
<p>
    Having a nutritious meal matters because it gives your body the nutrients it needs to function properly. It improves growth and development in kids. Additionally, it provides energy kids need for physical activities like sports. Overall, a nutritious meal gives your body the fuel, building materials, and protective nutrients it needs to stay healthy, grow, learn, and perform at its best.

</p>
</article>
